<title>UK: Weir wins gas ship system supply orders.</title>
<headline>Weir wins gas ship system supply orders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>British technology group Weir Group Plc said on Wednesday it had won contracts to supply cargo handling systems for three liquefied gas ships being built at Hyundai Heavy Industries' Ulsan shipyard.</p>
<p>In a statement the company said the contracts, worth $10 million, would cover the design and supply of systems.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
